{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"9cb8567a-e9ba-44d3-9c6a-254276473676","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The causes of the failure have been investigated, fixed in the codebase, and documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-UyDAXG/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Causes Found\n\n1. **`status` is a read-only variable in `zsh`**:\n   Line 19 of [bin/nightly-review.zsh](file:///tmp/h-UyDAXG/bin/nightly-review.zsh) attempted `status=$?`. In `zsh`, `status` is a special built-in variable and read-only. Assigning to it caused `zsh` to terminate immediately with fatal error `/Users/vk/bin/nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status`, killing the process before it could reach [bin/notify.sh](file:///tmp/h-UyDAXG/bin/notify.sh) to send failure alerts.\n2. **Missing `USER` in launchd environment**:\n   `launchd` runs jobs in a minimal environment. Without `USER` defined in `EnvironmentVariables`, `claude` could not resolve login credentials, causing every run to fail with `Not logged in · Please run /login` (as seen in [Library/Logs/nightly-review.err](file:///tmp/h-UyDAXG/Library/Logs/nightly-review.err)).\n\n### Fixes Applied\n\n- [bin/nightly-review.zsh](file:///tmp/h-UyDAXG/bin/nightly-review.zsh): Replaced `status=$?` with `rc=$?` (and updated downstream references), and piped the prompt via stdin (`print -r -- \"$PROMPT\" | claude -p ...`).\n- [Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist](file:///tmp/h-UyDAXG/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist): Added `\u003ckey\u003eUSER\u003c/key\u003e\u003cstring\u003evk\u003c/string\u003e` under `EnvironmentVariables`.\n- Detailed breakdown of which parts of the colleague's note applied vs. did not apply is recorded in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-UyDAXG/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":51.264025,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":162473,"output_tokens":2419,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":0,"total_tokens":164892}}}
